{"id": "sdqa0173", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.18, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4278, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": "February 15, 1820– March 13, 1906", "query": "When did Susan B. Anthony live?", "transcript": "When did Susan B Anthony live?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Susan and Anthony lived in a quiet valley beside a slow green river. Every morning they walked along the riverbank collecting smooth stones. One day they found a stone unlike any other. It was warm to the touch and glowed faintly. \"What's this?\" Susan asked, holding it up. Anthony looked at it closely. \"It feels special,\" he said. That night as they sat by the fire, the stone began to glow brighter. Suddenly a soft voice spoke, \"I am the guardian of the valley. You have freed me.\" The dragon appeared before them, not scary but kind and wise. From that day on, the two children and the small dragon became the best of friends, exploring the valley and protecting its secrets together.", "answer_ms": 4785}
